# Step 0 of issues/questions/2026-10-23-should-yo-add-a-flagless-cell.md:
# `RefCell.replace` moves the old value out, so it panics while a `with`
# body of the same cell runs, as Rust's `RefCell::replace` does under a live
# `borrow`. `build run` propagates the panic as rc≠0; the panic line ends in
# a machine-specific `(at file:///...)`, so only the diagnostic substring is
# kept.
stdout_keep_match=reading old|RefCell\.replace: the value is already borrowed \(a with, with_mut or replace_with body is running\)
timeout=300
